{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Close attempt (sanctioned non-force path) — STILL OPEN.\n\n1) 'rebar transition e5ec-2e8d-500a-4d2d open closed' failed with:\n   plan-review close gate: unsigned: no certified plan-review attestation. Run rebar review-plan e5ec-2e8d-500a-4d2d separately, then retry close.\n\n2) Ran the legitimate remedy 'rebar review-plan e5ec-2e8d-500a-4d2d' (no --force). Verdict: BLOCK (exit 1), 3 blocking findings, signature {signed: false, reason: BLOCK}. All three (E4, G6, T8) say the same thing: the plan's central premise — that a stale forced-tool / 'disable thinking' rationale 'still lingers' in runner.py and structured.py and 'reads as if forced-tool is still in use' — is refuted by the current source, which already says the opposite at both cited locations. The described defect does not exist any more.\n\nThe gate is blocking BECAUSE the work is already done: review-plan assesses a plan against current reality, so a delivered ticket's still-future-tense plan reads as divergent. Per the operator's instruction I used neither review-plan --force nor --force-close.\n\nTo unlock a close without a bypass: rewrite the Scope/Status text in the past tense (describing what WAS corrected, at the current anchors runner.py:99-108 and structured.py:11-16) and re-run review-plan — the documented 'when the acceptance criteria no longer match reality' remedy in docs/plan-review-gate.md. All three ACs are verified and ticked; only the plan-review close gate stands in the way."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786086582778368001,"uuid":"7dc7f07f-b1ca-4fbb-9f26-35da3a4530ee"}